.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt OSSL_MTC_CA_PARSE_CERTIFICATES 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_parse_certificates
.Nd load Merkle Tree Certificate authorities from certificates
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Lb libcrypto
.In openssl/mtc.h
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_parse_certificates
.Fa "void *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "STACK_OF(OSSL_MTC_CA) *out_cas"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Merkle Tree Certificate authority is represented as an X.509
certificate in the form of section 5.5 of the Merkle Tree Certificates
specification:
the subject is the CA's trust anchor identifier,
the subject public key is the CA cosigner's key,
and a critical extension carries the hash algorithm of the CA's logs
and the range of serial numbers it may issue.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_parse_certificates
reads PEM-encoded certificates from
.Fa in
until the end of input and adds to
.Fa out_cas
one
.Vt OSSL_MTC_CA
for each, with the CA's minimum and maximum serial numbers set from the
certificate.
PEM blocks that are not certificates are skipped.
.Fa out_cas
must have been created with
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_cmp 3
as its comparison function.
It fails if a certificate does not have the form above,
or if two CAs would have the same trust anchor identifier,
counting those already in
.Fa out_cas ;
in that case
.Fa out_cas
is unchanged.
.Fa libctx
and
.Fa propq
are ignored.
.Pp
The certificates are not verified.
The caller owns the
.Vt OSSL_MTC_CA
objects added to
.Fa out_cas
and frees them with
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_free 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_parse_certificates
returns 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BIO_new 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_find 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_new 3 ,
.Xr PEM_read_bio_X509 3
